('f2db0c30-a54f-518d-b3a9-2cb548008006','f4b4622a-133b-5ea0-a4a7-6a45330f0130',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to remove everything that is inside something','[ transitive ]',null,'برای حذف هر چیزی که درون چیزی است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Did you empty the dishwasher?","translation":"ماشین ظرفشویی رو خالی کردی؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645961.mp3"},{"sentence":"Elinor emptied the contents of the envelope onto the table.","translation":"الینور محتویات پاکت را روی میز خالی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645964.mp3"},{"sentence":"He emptied out the ashtray.","translation":"زیرسیگاری را خالی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001188173.mp3"},{"sentence":"Ruth emptied her glass (= drank all the liquid left in it ) in one gulp.","translation":"روت لیوان خود را (= تمام مایع باقیمانده در آن را نوشید) در یک جرعه خالی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000519.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('cecf501e-c313-5bb6-9bab-1e03196f2ceb','f4b4622a-133b-5ea0-a4a7-6a45330f0130',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if a place empties, everyone leaves it','[ intransitive ]',null,'اگر جایی خالی شود همه آن را ترک می کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The stores were closing, and the streets began to empty.","translation":"فروشگاه ها در حال بسته شدن بودند و خیابان ها شروع به خالی شدن کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001188187.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d5f85c46-5db5-5535-82ec-94e43d6fa597','603a3617-9247-54c7-9923-94a5e947fab5',1,null,null,'spoken & written','someone who hates you and wants to harm you',null,null,'دشمن، خصم؛ دشمن (سپاهی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a great enemy Henry prepared to fight his great enemy, the king of France.','a main/biggest/greatest enemy Terrorism is our country’s main enemy.','an arch enemy (= main enemy, used for emphasis ) The comic book character Lex Luthor is Superman’s arch enemy.','bitter enemies (= enemies who hate each other very much ) When these former friends quarrelled over money, they became bitter enemies.','sworn enemies (= enemies who will always hate each other ) The men have been sworn enemies for many years.','a formidable enemy (= a very powerful enemy ) The North Vietnamese army proved to be a formidable enemy.','deadly enemies (= enemies who try to harm each other as much as possible ) France and Germany, once deadly enemies, are now partners in the European Union.','an old/traditional enemy (= one you have had a long time ) In 1548, Scotland moved towards an alliance with her traditional enemy, England.','a common enemy (= one shared by groups of people ) We must work together against the common enemy.','a political enemy the prime minister’s political enemies','make enemies (= become unfriendly with people ) During her long and turbulent career, she made many enemies.','defend/protect yourself from your enemies Our country has a right to protect itself from its enemies.','defeat the enemy We will never defeat our enemies unless we stop fighting each other.','an enemy force (= a military group that is your enemy ) The town is occupied by enemy forces.','an enemy position (= a place controlled by an enemy army ) General Hunt ordered an air strike on the enemy positions.','behind enemy lines (= behind the edge of an area that is controlled by an enemy army ) Men from the First Airborne Division were dropped behind enemy lines.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She’s a dangerous enemy to have.","translation":"او یک دشمن خطرناک برای داشتن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001192613.mp3"},{"sentence":"Cats and dogs have always been natural enemies .","translation":"گربه ها و سگ ها همیشه دشمنان طبیعی بوده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001678315.mp3"},{"sentence":"an old enemy of her father","translation":"دشمن قدیمی پدرش","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001678319.mp3"},{"sentence":"a ruthless businessman who made a lot of enemies","translation":"یک تاجر بی رحم که دشمنان زیادی پیدا کرد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001192620.mp3"},{"sentence":"the unforgettable sight of the president shaking hands with his sworn enemy (= an enemy you will always hate )","translation":"منظره فراموش نشدنی رئیس جمهور در حال دست دادن با دشمن قسم خورده خود (= دشمنی که همیشه از آن متنفر خواهید بود)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001678323.mp3"},{"sentence":"I wouldn’t wish this on my worst enemy .","translation":"من این را برای بدترین دشمنم آرزو نمی کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001678330.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('7c24c279-ca9f-5fe2-94c0-654838f132b2','603a3617-9247-54c7-9923-94a5e947fab5',2,null,null,'spoken & written','someone who opposes or competes against you',null,null,'کسی که با شما مخالف است یا با شما رقابت می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a great enemy Henry prepared to fight his great enemy, the king of France.','a main/biggest/greatest enemy Terrorism is our country’s main enemy.','an arch enemy (= main enemy, used for emphasis ) The comic book character Lex Luthor is Superman’s arch enemy.','bitter enemies (= enemies who hate each other very much ) When these former friends quarrelled over money, they became bitter enemies.','sworn enemies (= enemies who will always hate each other ) The men have been sworn enemies for many years.','a formidable enemy (= a very powerful enemy ) The North Vietnamese army proved to be a formidable enemy.','deadly enemies (= enemies who try to harm each other as much as possible ) France and Germany, once deadly enemies, are now partners in the European Union.','an old/traditional enemy (= one you have had a long time ) In 1548, Scotland moved towards an alliance with her traditional enemy, England.','a common enemy (= one shared by groups of people ) We must work together against the common enemy.','a political enemy the prime minister’s political enemies','make enemies (= become unfriendly with people ) During her long and turbulent career, she made many enemies.','defend/protect yourself from your enemies Our country has a right to protect itself from its enemies.','defeat the enemy We will never defeat our enemies unless we stop fighting each other.','an enemy force (= a military group that is your enemy ) The town is occupied by enemy forces.','an enemy position (= a place controlled by an enemy army ) General Hunt ordered an air strike on the enemy positions.','behind enemy lines (= behind the edge of an area that is controlled by an enemy army ) Men from the First Airborne Division were dropped behind enemy lines.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"political enemies","translation":"دشمنان سیاسی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001192627.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was imprisoned for being ‘an enemy of the revolution’.","translation":"او به جرم «دشمن انقلاب» به زندان افتاد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001192628.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('62380bde-f7ab-5359-a6fa-76f0539f647f','603a3617-9247-54c7-9923-94a5e947fab5',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the country against which your country is fighting in a war',null,null,'کشوری که کشور شما در حال جنگ علیه آن است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a great enemy Henry prepared to fight his great enemy, the king of France.','a main/biggest/greatest enemy Terrorism is our country’s main enemy.','an arch enemy (= main enemy, used for emphasis ) The comic book character Lex Luthor is Superman’s arch enemy.','bitter enemies (= enemies who hate each other very much ) When these former friends quarrelled over money, they became bitter enemies.','sworn enemies (= enemies who will always hate each other ) The men have been sworn enemies for many years.','a formidable enemy (= a very powerful enemy ) The North Vietnamese army proved to be a formidable enemy.','deadly enemies (= enemies who try to harm each other as much as possible ) France and Germany, once deadly enemies, are now partners in the European Union.','an old/traditional enemy (= one you have had a long time ) In 1548, Scotland moved towards an alliance with her traditional enemy, England.','a common enemy (= one shared by groups of people ) We must work together against the common enemy.','a political enemy the prime minister’s political enemies','make enemies (= become unfriendly with people ) During her long and turbulent career, she made many enemies.','defend/protect yourself from your enemies Our country has a right to protect itself from its enemies.','defeat the enemy We will never defeat our enemies unless we stop fighting each other.','an enemy force (= a military group that is your enemy ) The town is occupied by enemy forces.','an enemy position (= a place controlled by an enemy army ) General Hunt ordered an air strike on the enemy positions.','behind enemy lines (= behind the edge of an area that is controlled by an enemy army ) Men from the First Airborne Division were dropped behind enemy lines.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He was accused of collaboration with the enemy.","translation":"متهم به همکاری با دشمن شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001831936.mp3"},{"sentence":"a town behind enemy lines","translation":"شهری در پشت خطوط دشمن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001192639.mp3"},{"sentence":"The enemy was defeated.","translation":"دشمن شکست خورد.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"The enemy were defeated.","translation":"دشمن شکست خورد.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,4),
('86602549-4478-513b-9cc5-353b8d837fe4','603a3617-9247-54c7-9923-94a5e947fab5',4,null,null,'spoken & written','something that people think is harmful or damaging',null,null,'چیزی که مردم فکر می کنند مضر یا مضر است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The usual enemies, cigarettes and alcohol, are targeted for tax rises.","translation":"دشمنان معمولی، سیگار و الکل، هدف افزایش مالیات هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001678343.mp3"},{"sentence":"The common enemy that united them was racial inequality.","translation":"دشمن مشترکی که آنها را متحد کرد، نابرابری نژادی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001678344.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
