 to help the people in it deal with a difficult time ) She set up a support group for people suffering from the same illness.','a control group (= a group used in an experiment or survey to compare its results with those of another group ) A control group had to be examined as well as the group that we are studying.','a group decision Being involved in a group decision can help motivate workers.','a group discussion The course includes both individual work and group discussions.','a group leader There were three groups of eight people, each with a group leader.','belong to a group Ben belonged to an environmental group.','get into groups The teacher asked the students to get into groups.','organize something into groups Small children work best when they are organized into very small groups.','join a group He joined a self-help group for divorced men.','leave a group Rebecca left the group following a disagreement.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a left-wing terrorist group","translation":"یک گروه تروریستی چپ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702133.mp3"},{"sentence":"She is one of a group of women who have suffered severe side-effects from the drug.","translation":"او یکی از آن دسته از زنانی است که دچار عوارض جانبی شدید این دارو شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001305908.mp3"},{"sentence":"Minority groups are encouraged to apply.","translation":"گروه های اقلیت تشویق می شوند که درخواست دهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702134.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
