('33a1e063-aeba-5394-9e64-9de0edf4b8bd','08cd3476-53cc-53a6-913c-4bb4abfe48bf',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'guess what/you’ll never guess who/what etc','حدس زدن؛ حدس، گمان (درباره)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('41f6c7ed-1096-53da-9e42-2ab3196d0acd','d34150f5-d7fa-578b-b7eb-6eede576f3fb',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an attempt to answer a question or make a judgment when you are not sure whether you will be correct',null,null,'حدس، گمان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a guess I didn''t know the answer to question 7, so I just had to make a guess.','have a guess British English , take a guess American English: Go on, have a guess at how much it cost. Take a guess. How many people do you think showed up?','hazard a guess (= guess something, when you feel very uncertain ) No one at this stage is prepared to hazard a guess about the outcome of the elections.','a rough guess (= one that is not exact ) This is just a rough guess, but I think it would cost about $50.','a wild guess (= one made without much thought or information ) I made a wild guess and I got the answer right first time.','a lucky guess ‘How did you know?’ ‘It was just a lucky guess.’','a good guess (= one that is likely to be right ) I''m not sure how old she is, but I can make a good guess!','somebody’s best guess (= one that you think is most likely to be right ) My best guess is that it will take around six months.','an educated/informed guess (= a guess based on things that you know are correct ) Stockbrokers try to make educated guesses as to which stocks will do well.','an intelligent guess Analysis of the archaeological site will help us make an intelligent guess as to what it was used for.','an inspired guess (= a very good guess that you make suddenly ) It’s hard to believe he got that right with just an inspired guess.','my guess is (that) My guess is there won’t be many people there.','at a guess British English (= used when saying that you are making a guess ) I''d say it was built around the turn of the century, at a guess.','I’ll give you three guesses (= used to tell someone that it should be easy for them to guess the answer to their question ) ‘Where is he?’ ‘I’ll give you three guesses.’']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’d say she’s about 35, but that’s only a guess.","translation":"من می توانم بگویم او حدود 35 سال دارد، اما این فقط یک حدس است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000736.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('857b2f66-8648-5784-9fb4-344f0cdee60f','d34150f5-d7fa-578b-b7eb-6eede576f3fb',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be anybody’s guess','حدس، گمان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a guess I didn''t know the answer to question 7, so I just had to make a guess.','have a guess British English , take a guess American English: Go on, have a guess at how much it cost. Take a guess. How many people do you think showed up?','hazard a guess (= guess something, when you feel very uncertain ) No one at this stage is prepared to hazard a guess about the outcome of the elections.','a rough guess (= one that is not exact ) This is just a rough guess, but I think it would cost about $50.','a wild guess (= one made without much thought or information ) I made a wild guess and I got the answer right first time.','a lucky guess ‘How did you know?’ ‘It was just a lucky guess.’','a good guess (= one that is likely to be right ) I''m not sure how old she is, but I can make a good guess!','somebody’s best guess (= one that you think is most likely to be right ) My best guess is that it will take around six months.','an educated/informed guess (= a guess based on things that you know are correct ) Stockbrokers try to make educated guesses as to which stocks will do well.','an intelligent guess Analysis of the archaeological site will help us make an intelligent guess as to what it was used for.','an inspired guess (= a very good guess that you make suddenly ) It’s hard to believe he got that right with just an inspired guess.','my guess is (that) My guess is there won’t be many people there.','at a guess British English (= used when saying that you are making a guess ) I''d say it was built around the turn of the century, at a guess.','I’ll give you three guesses (= used to tell someone that it should be easy for them to guess the answer to their question ) ‘Where is he?’ ‘I’ll give you three guesses.’']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('0c1820bf-0e1d-5d2a-960f-f06941dcfa18','d34150f5-d7fa-578b-b7eb-6eede576f3fb',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'your guess is as good as mine','حدس، گمان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a guess I didn''t know the answer to question 7, so I just had to make a guess.','have a guess British English , take a guess American English: Go on, have a guess at how much it cost. Take a guess. How many people do you think showed up?','hazard a guess (= guess something, when you feel very uncertain ) No one at this stage is prepared to hazard a guess about the outcome of the elections.','a rough guess (= one that is not exact ) This is just a rough guess, but I think it would cost about $50.','a wild guess (= one made without much thought or information ) I made a wild guess and I got the answer right first time.','a lucky guess ‘How did you know?’ ‘It was just a lucky guess.’','a good guess (= one that is likely to be right ) I''m not sure how old she is, but I can make a good guess!','somebody’s best guess (= one that you think is most likely to be right ) My best guess is that it will take around six months.','an educated/informed guess (= a guess based on things that you know are correct ) Stockbrokers try to make educated guesses as to which stocks will do well.','an intelligent guess Analysis of the archaeological site will help us make an intelligent guess as to what it was used for.','an inspired guess (= a very good guess that you make suddenly ) It’s hard to believe he got that right with just an inspired guess.','my guess is (that) My guess is there won’t be many people there.','at a guess British English (= used when saying that you are making a guess ) I''d say it was built around the turn of the century, at a guess.','I’ll give you three guesses (= used to tell someone that it should be easy for them to guess the answer to their question ) ‘Where is he?’ ‘I’ll give you three guesses.’']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5735a21f-7d23-5288-af21-e4e26f50b247','b6fe7bc2-2bce-5858-a7dc-49c166feb437',1,'at an event','در یک رویداد','spoken & written','someone who is invited to an event or special occasion',null,null,'مهمان؛ مهمان (ویژه)؛ مهمان (فرضی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the main/chief/principal guest The prime minister was one of the main guests at the event.','an honoured guest (= one who is given special respect and treatment ) They were the honoured guests of the Queen at the Royal Garden Party.','a distinguished guest (= one who has done something that people respect or admire ) Many distinguished guests were invited to the opening ceremony.','dinner guests How much meat do I need to buy for 15 dinner guests?','wedding guests We need to send out invitations to all the wedding guests.','a house guest (= someone who is staying in your house ) There was a constant stream of house guests at their country estate.','invited guests Celebrations continued with a dinner for 100 invited guests.','an unwelcome guest (= someone who is not really a guest, and whom you do not want at an event ) Security guards were employed to keep out unwelcome guests.','an uninvited guest She was surprised when an uninvited guest turned up at the door.','a regular/frequent guest The Johnsons were regular guests at Eric’s house in Notting Hill.','the guest list (= a list of the people invited to an event ) The guest list included many friends from his university days.','a guest speaker/lecturer (= one who is invited to an event from another organization, university etc ) The guest speaker at the conference was Dr. Kim.','the guest of honour (= the most important guest ) The senator was guest of honour at a reception held at the American Embassy.','invite a guest The guests were invited to a dinner at his country house.','greet the guests Roger was busy greeting the guests as they arrived.','entertain guests (= have guests at your house or another place for a meal or party ) Their garden is a wonderful place to entertain guests.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a banquet for 250 distinguished guests","translation":"یک ضیافت برای 250 مهمان برجسته","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702619.mp3"},{"sentence":"You are here as my guests.","translation":"شما به عنوان مهمان من اینجا هستید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702620.mp3"},{"sentence":"Most of the wedding guests had left.","translation":"بیشتر مهمانان عروسی رفته بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702628.mp3"},{"sentence":"Among the invited guests were Jerry Brown and Elihu Harris.","translation":"جری براون و الیهو هریس از جمله مهمانان دعوت شده بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702629.mp3"},{"sentence":"The actress was guest of honour (= the most important guest ) at the launch.","translation":"این بازیگر در مراسم افتتاحیه مهمان افتخاری (= مهمترین مهمان) بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702633.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ve nearly finished the guest list for the wedding.","translation":"من تقریبا لیست مهمانان عروسی را تمام کرده ام.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702638.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’ re having some people over for dinner this evening.","translation":"امروز عصر چند نفر را برای شام می‌خوریم.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,7),
('2c318281-ce90-588d-bd62-20fe6e9737d0','b6fe7bc2-2bce-5858-a7dc-49c166feb437',2,'in a house','در یک خانه','spoken & written','someone you have invited to stay in your home for a short time',null,'house guest','کسی را که دعوت کرده اید برای مدت کوتاهی در خانه شما بماند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the main/chief/principal guest The prime minister was one of the main guests at the event.','an honoured guest (= one who is given special respect and treatment ) They were the honoured guests of the Queen at the Royal Garden Party.','a distinguished guest (= one who has done something that people respect or admire ) Many distinguished guests were invited to the opening ceremony.','dinner guests How much meat do I need to buy for 15 dinner guests?','wedding guests We need to send out invitations to all the wedding guests.','a house guest (= someone who is staying in your house ) There was a constant stream of house guests at their country estate.','invited guests Celebrations continued with a dinner for 100 invited guests.','an unwelcome guest (= someone who is not really a guest, and whom you do not want at an event ) Security guards were employed to keep out unwelcome guests.','an uninvited guest She was surprised when an uninvited guest turned up at the door.','a regular/frequent guest The Johnsons were regular guests at Eric’s house in Notting Hill.','the guest list (= a list of the people invited to an event ) The guest list included many friends from his university days.','a guest speaker/lecturer (= one who is invited to an event from another organization, university etc ) The guest speaker at the conference was Dr. Kim.','the guest of honour (= the most important guest ) The senator was guest of honour at a reception held at the American Embassy.','invite a guest The guests were invited to a dinner at his country house.','greet the guests Roger was busy greeting the guests as they arrived.','entertain guests (= have guests at your house or another place for a meal or party ) Their garden is a wonderful place to entertain guests.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We have guests staying right now.","translation":"ما در حال حاضر مهمان داریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702642.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6ace9d6f-33dc-5182-bf14-ba23e98b4176','b6fe7bc2-2bce-5858-a7dc-49c166feb437',3,'in a hotel','در یک هتل','spoken & written','someone who is paying to stay in a hotel',null,null,'کسی که برای اقامت در هتل پول می دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Use of the sauna is free to guests.","translation":"استفاده از سونا برای مهمانان رایگان است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001309915.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c21887b0-efa3-56eb-94bc-3843ce73f2f7','b6fe7bc2-2bce-5858-a7dc-49c166feb437',4,'on a show','در یک نمایش','spoken & written','someone famous who is invited to take part in a show, concert etc, in addition to those who usually take part',null,null,'شخص مشهوری که برای شرکت در یک نمایش، کنسرت و غیره دعوت می شود، علاوه بر کسانی که معمولاً شرکت می کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We have some great guests for you tonight.","translation":"امشب برای شما مهمانان خوبی داریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702646.mp3"},{"sentence":"Fontaine appeared as a guest on the show.","translation":"فونتین به عنوان مهمان در برنامه ظاهر شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702647.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('271a4107-8529-5b80-bbaa-e5b879c87afd','b6fe7bc2-2bce-5858-a7dc-49c166feb437',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be my guest','مهمان؛ مهمان (ویژه)؛ مهمان (فرضی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1434d18c-602f-55ef-a9ee-3e558346d90d','2f56a2a0-b490-5944-a02c-0bde4a0ac581',1,null,null,'spoken & written','for guests to use',null,null,'برای استفاده مهمانان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He was still asleep in the guest bedroom.","translation":"او هنوز در اتاق خواب مهمان خواب بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702768.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d36840d7-7096-52b1-9435-cd85965271e8','2f56a2a0-b490-5944-a02c-0bde4a0ac581',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a guest star , speaker etc is someone famous or important who is invited to take part in an event, in addition to the people who usually take part',null,null,'ستاره مهمان، سخنران و غیره شخص مشهور یا مهمی است که علاوه بر افرادی که معمولاً در یک رویداد شرکت می کنند، دعوت می شود.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Camfield was lucky in getting Cage and Rampling as guest stars.","translation":"کمفیلد خوش شانس بود که کیج و رمپلینگ را به عنوان ستاره های مهمان انتخاب کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702775.mp3"},{"sentence":"He will make a special guest appearance on next week’s show.","translation":"او یک مهمان ویژه در برنامه هفته آینده خواهد داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702779.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('52a5ddbf-0f6d-5357-808b-11eeea02a5c6','454d5170-9160-5f3e-9574-df4406c4c5fa',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to take part in a show, concert etc as a guest',null,null,'برای شرکت در یک نمایش، کنسرت و غیره به عنوان مهمان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She guested on a comedy show last year.","translation":"او سال گذشته در یک برنامه کمدی مهمان بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702653.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('cd79bd96-9c43-531c-b864-96a271c32488','7b85ae22-b861-5610-90cf-1df01de85223',1,'for deciding/judging','برای تصمیم گیری/قضاوت','spoken & written','something that provides information and helps you to form an opinion or make a decision',null,null,'راهنما، راهنمای (کتاب)؛ معیار؛ رهنمود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The polls are not a reliable guide of how people will vote.","translation":"نظرسنجی ها راهنمای قابل اعتمادی برای نحوه رأی دادن مردم نیستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001310100.mp3"},{"sentence":"The figures are only a rough guide .","translation":"ارقام فقط یک راهنمای تقریبی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702667.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8baea8e6-185e-5b6b-8622-1a3e1b7b0755','7b85ae22-b861-5610-90cf-1df01de85223',2,'person','شخص','spoken & written','someone whose job is to take tourists to a place and show them around',null,null,'کسی که کارش بردن گردشگران به مکانی و نشان دادن آنها است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a tour guide","translation":"یک راهنمای تور","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702671.mp3"},{"sentence":"an experienced mountain guide","translation":"یک راهنمای کوهستانی با تجربه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702672.mp3"},{"sentence":"my spiritual guide","translation":"راهنمای معنوی من","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001310093.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('2c70df38-4386-590f-9b98-608bdba502ed','7b85ae22-b861-5610-90cf-1df01de85223',3,'instructions','دستورالعمل ها','spoken & written','a book or piece of writing that provides information on a particular subject or explains how to do something',null,null,'کتاب یا نوشته‌ای که اطلاعاتی در مورد موضوع خاصی ارائه می‌کند یا نحوه انجام کاری را توضیح می‌دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a guide to North American birds","translation":"راهنمای پرندگان آمریکای شمالی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001310109.mp3"},{"sentence":"Follow our step-by-step guide .","translation":"راهنمای گام به گام ما را دنبال کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702675.mp3"},{"sentence":"Details of how to use the various programs are in the user guide .","translation":"جزئیات نحوه استفاده از برنامه های مختلف در راهنمای کاربر موجود است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702679.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('39b81808-551d-52ef-b412-0b81b11aad6c','7b85ae22-b861-5610-90cf-1df01de85223',4,'girl','دختر','spoken & written','the Guides Association , which teaches girls practical skills',null,null,'انجمن راهنماها که به دختران مهارت های عملی را آموزش می دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8c94326d-6ae3-5ef5-997e-beb01ce6459e','17b7658b-415e-585b-9536-917e51b89ce6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to take someone to a place',null,null,'هدایت کردن، راهنمایی کردن؛ پیش بردن (دست)',array['lead']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He guided us through the narrow streets to the central mosque.","translation":"از کوچه های باریک ما را به سمت مسجد مرکزی راهنمایی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001310134.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5f56c17e-d92c-5a4e-8899-cbebd4af779c','17b7658b-415e-585b-9536-917e51b89ce6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to help someone or something to move in a particular direction',null,null,'کمک کردن به کسی یا چیزی برای حرکت در جهتی خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He guided her firmly towards the sofa.","translation":"او را محکم به سمت مبل راهنمایی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001310138.mp3"},{"sentence":"Searchlights were used to guide the ship into the harbour.","translation":"از چراغ های جستجو برای هدایت کشتی به بندر استفاده شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702682.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c3821f77-f159-55b7-aca8-9a51bdc893a2','17b7658b-415e-585b-9536-917e51b89ce6',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to influence someone’s behaviour or ideas',null,null,'تأثیر گذاشتن بر رفتار یا عقاید کسی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Teenagers need adults to guide them.","translation":"نوجوانان به بزرگسالان نیاز دارند که آنها را راهنمایی کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702683.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d53839d5-b7c0-51e2-a8d2-94277371e982','17b7658b-415e-585b-9536-917e51b89ce6',4,null,null,'spoken & written','to show someone the right way to do something, especially something difficult or complicated',null,null,'به کسی نشان دادن راه درست برای انجام کاری، به خصوص کاری دشوار یا پیچیده','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Guide your students through the program one section at a time.","translation":"دانش آموزان خود را در برنامه یک بخش در یک زمان راهنمایی کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001310148.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a1e25eed-d1f9-5a50-9c9e-e02634f33b2b','d9e65040-4d41-5d04-a43d-e9c036aef14b',1,'usual/regular','معمولی/معمولی','spoken & written','something that you do regularly or usually, often without thinking about it because you have done it so many times before','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'عادت، خو؛ عادت (رفتاری)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a habit (of doing something) He has a habit of being late.','something becomes a habit Once you have been driving for a few weeks, it becomes a habit.','get into a habit (= start doing something regularly or often ) Try to get into the habit of walking for 30 minutes each day.','get out of a habit (= stop doing something regularly or often ) She couldn’t get out of the habit of saying ''sorry''.','break/kick a habit (= stop doing something that is bad for you ) I’ve smoked for years, but I really want to kick the habit.','develop/form a habit I developed a habit of eating porridge for breakfast.','change your habits It''s sometimes difficult for people to change their habits.','a good/bad habit Eating healthy food as snacks is a good habit to get into.','eating/drinking habits (= the kinds of things you eat or drink regularly ) You need to change your eating habits.','buying/spending habits (= the kinds of things you buy regularly ) The recession will mean that many people will be changing their spending habits.','viewing habits (= the kinds of television shows you regularly watch ) Parents try to control their children’s viewing habits.','sexual habits (= what you normally do in sexual relationships ) a survey of the sexual habits of gay men','personal habits (= the things you normally do each day, for example keeping yourself clean or whether you smoke ) Some of his personal habits were unpleasant.','social habits (= the things people normally do when they are with other people ) Television changed some of our social habits.','an annoying/unpleasant/nasty habit He had the unpleasant habit of eating with his mouth open.','a strange/peculiar/odd habit He had a lot of peculiar habits, one of them being to stare at you without blinking.','be in the habit of doing something On Friday evenings, Carrie was in the habit of visiting her parents.','(by/from) force of habit (= used about a habit that is difficult to change ) I still walk by his house each day - force of habit, I suppose.','change/break the habits of a lifetime (= stop doing the things you have done for many years ) It is hard to change the habits of a lifetime, but you must eat more healthily or you will have a heart attack.','have the unfortunate habit of doing something (= do something that makes other people feel embarrassed or offended ) Teenage girls have the unfortunate habit of laughing too loudly.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Regular exercise is a good habit.","translation":"ورزش منظم یک عادت خوب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000739.mp3"},{"sentence":"Thinking negatively can become a habit.","translation":"منفی اندیشی می تواند به یک عادت تبدیل شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001967489.mp3"},{"sentence":"She has a habit of playing with her hair when she’s nervous.","translation":"او عادت دارد وقتی عصبی است با موهایش بازی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001967497.mp3"},{"sentence":"Some people drink alcohol as much from habit as from desire.","translation":"برخی افراد به همان اندازه که از روی عادت الکل می نوشند، از روی میل.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001967515.mp3"},{"sentence":"I did it out of habit.","translation":"من از روی عادت این کار را کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040083.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('cf857e7f-80ef-5716-afe6-8c479a164895','d9e65040-4d41-5d04-a43d-e9c036aef14b',2,'drugs','مواد مخدر','spoken & written','a strong physical need to keep taking a drug regularly','[ countable ]',null,'نیاز فیزیکی شدید به مصرف منظم دارو','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a habit (of doing something) He has a habit of being late.','something becomes a habit Once you have been driving for a few weeks, it becomes a habit.','get into a habit (= start doing something regularly or often ) Try to get into the habit of walking for 30 minutes each day.','get out of a habit (= stop doing something regularly or often ) She couldn’t get out of the habit of saying ''sorry''.','break/kick a habit (= stop doing something that is bad for you ) I’ve smoked for years, but I really want to kick the habit.','develop/form a habit I developed a habit of eating porridge for breakfast.','change your habits It''s sometimes difficult for people to change their habits.','a good/bad habit Eating healthy food as snacks is a good habit to get into.','eating/drinking habits (= the kinds of things you eat or drink regularly ) You need to change your eating habits.','buying/spending habits (= the kinds of things you buy regularly ) The recession will mean that many people will be changing their spending habits.','viewing habits (= the kinds of television shows you regularly watch ) Parents try to control their children’s viewing habits.','sexual habits (= what you normally do in sexual relationships ) a survey of the sexual habits of gay men','personal habits (= the things you normally do each day, for example keeping yourself clean or whether you smoke ) Some of his personal habits were unpleasant.','social habits (= the things people normally do when they are with other people ) Television changed some of our social habits.','an annoying/unpleasant/nasty habit He had the unpleasant habit of eating with his mouth open.','a strange/peculiar/odd habit He had a lot of peculiar habits, one of them being to stare at you without blinking.','be in the habit of doing something On Friday evenings, Carrie was in the habit of visiting her parents.','(by/from) force of habit (= used about a habit that is difficult to change ) I still walk by his house each day - force of habit, I suppose.','change/break the habits of a lifetime (= stop doing the things you have done for many years ) It is hard to change the habits of a lifetime, but you must eat more healthily or you will have a heart attack.','have the unfortunate habit of doing something (= do something that makes other people feel embarrassed or offended ) Teenage girls have the unfortunate habit of laughing too loudly.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"A lot of drug addicts get into petty crime to support their habit.","translation":"بسیاری از معتادان به مواد مخدر برای حمایت از عادت خود دست به جرایم کوچک می زنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001367842.mp3"},{"sentence":"His cocaine habit ruined him physically and financially.","translation":"عادت به مصرف کوکائین او را از نظر جسمی و مالی خراب کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001367845.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
