('ba0c5794-0d4d-5cf3-ad7e-8355e6840cd6','95eec8cc-b063-59ef-ac39-1221f7ad8338',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to provide someone with a place to live',null,null,'فراهم کردن مکانی برای زندگی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The refugees are being housed in temporary accommodation.","translation":"پناهندگان در اسکان موقت اسکان داده می شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001362998.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('8f8a1e4b-0e75-537e-942a-10895133a968','95eec8cc-b063-59ef-ac39-1221f7ad8338',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if a building, place, or container houses something, it is kept there',null,null,'اگر ساختمان، مکان یا ظرفی چیزی را در خود جای دهد، در آنجا نگهداری می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The collection is currently housed in the British Museum.","translation":"این مجموعه در حال حاضر در موزه بریتانیا نگهداری می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001363002.mp3"},{"sentence":"the plastic case that houses the batteries","translation":"جعبه پلاستیکی که باتری ها را در خود جای داده است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020090.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('3de4f49f-b2fb-52b1-aa8d-d7dfed4ab945','88711d59-de7f-5ece-89ba-94517bff7a4d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','belonging to or relating to people, especially as opposed to machines or animals',null,null,'انسانی، انسانی‌دوست؛ انسانی (بدن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the human body The diagram shows all the organs in the human body.','the human mind/brain Distances in space are too great for the human mind to comprehend.','the human spirit Our capacity for forgiveness is a triumph of the human spirit.','the human eye (= used especially when saying that something cannot be seen by people ) These creatures are too small for the human eye to see.','human life I firmly believe in the sanctity of all human life.','human health Toxic waste is a risk to human health and the environment.','human behaviour British English , human behavior American English We study the aspects of human behaviour that result from our social upbringing.','human activity Our research measured the impact of human activity on this particular eco-system.','human relationships Trust is an essential ingredient in all human relationships.','human society In every human society there is a struggle for power.','the human population The UN estimates that the human population will reach 9.1 billion by 2050.','human error Investigators concluded that the crash was caused by human error.','human needs (= the things people need to have in order to live a normal healthy comfortable life ) The islanders meet the universal basic human needs of food and shelter in unexpected ways.','human remains (= the body of someone who has died ) The police found human remains in the basement.','for human consumption/habitation (= to be eaten/lived in by people ) This meat is not fit for human consumption.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There are many different cell types in the human body .","translation":"انواع مختلفی از سلول ها در بدن انسان وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001967392.mp3"},{"sentence":"the power of the human mind","translation":"قدرت ذهن انسان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001720815.mp3"},{"sentence":"The desire for joy lies deep within the human spirit .","translation":"میل به شادی در اعماق روح انسان نهفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001720846.mp3"},{"sentence":"Infra-red light is invisible to the human eye .","translation":"نور مادون قرمز برای چشم انسان نامرئی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001967400.mp3"},{"sentence":"theories of human behaviour","translation":"نظریه های رفتار انسان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001967404.mp3"},{"sentence":"different areas of human experience","translation":"حوزه های مختلف تجربه انسانی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001720821.mp3"},{"sentence":"respect for the absolute value of human life","translation":"احترام به ارزش مطلق زندگی انسان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001720824.mp3"},{"sentence":"The accident was the result of human error .","translation":"این حادثه نتیجه خطای انسانی بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001364638.mp3"},{"sentence":"The meat was declared unfit for human consumption .","translation":"گوشت برای مصرف انسان نامناسب اعلام شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000549492.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
('da453cd4-7cc3-55c4-bf4b-b5f802ce28a2','88711d59-de7f-5ece-89ba-94517bff7a4d',2,null,null,'spoken & written','human weaknesses , emotions etc are those that are typical of people',null,null,'ضعف‌های انسانی، احساسات و غیره آن‌هایی هستند که برای مردم عادی هستند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the human body The diagram shows all the organs in the human body.','the human mind/brain Distances in space are too great for the human mind to comprehend.','the human spirit Our capacity for forgiveness is a triumph of the human spirit.','the human eye (= used especially when saying that something cannot be seen by people ) These creatures are too small for the human eye to see.','human life I firmly believe in the sanctity of all human life.','human health Toxic waste is a risk to human health and the environment.','human behaviour British English , human behavior American English We study the aspects of human behaviour that result from our social upbringing.','human activity Our research measured the impact of human activity on this particular eco-system.','human relationships Trust is an essential ingredient in all human relationships.','human society In every human society there is a struggle for power.','the human population The UN estimates that the human population will reach 9.1 billion by 2050.','human error Investigators concluded that the crash was caused by human error.','human needs (= the things people need to have in order to live a normal healthy comfortable life ) The islanders meet the universal basic human needs of food and shelter in unexpected ways.','human remains (= the body of someone who has died ) The police found human remains in the basement.','for human consumption/habitation (= to be eaten/lived in by people ) This meat is not fit for human consumption.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He was also a person with very obvious human failings.","translation":"او همچنین فردی با نقص های انسانی بسیار آشکار بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001364642.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
