('e20313f4-40a6-5503-8295-8288098a2035','c3ae5491-923d-58ed-805e-93b4e76479d5',1,'opinion','نظر','spoken & written','to form or give an opinion about someone or something after thinking carefully about all the information you know about them','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'داوری کردن، قضاوت کردن (پس از سنجش)؛ ارزیابی کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be difficult/hard to judge The economic results of the reforms are difficult to judge.','be impossible to judge How much this affected their children was impossible to judge.','judge something objectively (= by looking at the facts ) His behaviour, judged objectively by what he has done, is dishonest.','judge somebody harshly (= in a severe or unkind way ) Do not judge her too harshly; she was very young at the time.','judge something correctly It takes a lot of experience to judge correctly what is needed.','judge something a success/failure (= consider it to be a success/failure ) The concert was judged a success.','judge something on its merits (= according to what you see when you look at it, rather than what people tell you ) The arguments should be judged on their merits.','judge something on the basis of something (= by considering something ) It is difficult to judge progress on the basis of a single day.','judge it best/better to do something (= think that something is the best thing to do ) Robert wanted to go and help him, but judged it best to stay where he was.','judge it safe to do something (= consider that it is safe to do something ) He listened for some time before judging it safe to go downstairs.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"You should never judge a person by their looks.","translation":"هرگز نباید یک نفر را از روی ظاهرش قضاوت کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001430558.mp3"},{"sentence":"Judge us on the improvements we make in the economy.","translation":"ما را در مورد پیشرفت هایی که در اقتصاد انجام می دهیم قضاوت کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001430561.mp3"},{"sentence":"The therapist judged that Margaret had made a serious attempt to kill herself.","translation":"درمانگر قضاوت کرد که مارگارت تلاش جدی برای خودکشی انجام داده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000872.mp3"},{"sentence":"pollutants that were judged hazardous to human health","translation":"آلاینده هایی که برای سلامتی انسان خطرناک ارزیابی می شوند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001973808.mp3"},{"sentence":"I am in no position to judge whether what she is doing is right or wrong.","translation":"من در موقعیتی نیستم که قضاوت کنم که آیا کاری که او انجام می دهد درست یا غلط است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001973811.mp3"},{"sentence":"The economic results of the reforms are very difficult to judge .","translation":"قضاوت در مورد نتایج اقتصادی اصلاحات بسیار دشوار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001730297.mp3"},{"sentence":"The likelihood of future bombs was impossible to judge .","translation":"قضاوت در مورد احتمال بمب های آینده غیرممکن بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001973815.mp3"},{"sentence":"We judge the success of a product by the number of sales it brings in.","translation":"ما موفقیت یک محصول را بر اساس تعداد فروش آن قضاوت می کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001973819.mp3"},{"sentence":"His conduct, judged objectively by what he has done, is dishonest.","translation":"رفتار او که به طور عینی بر اساس کاری که انجام داده است مورد قضاوت قرار می گیرد، ناصادقانه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001973823.mp3"},{"sentence":"Robert wanted to go and help him, but judged it best to stay where he was.","translation":"رابرت می خواست برود و به او کمک کند، اما بهترین قضاوت را داشت که همانجا بماند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001430576.mp3"},{"sentence":"Do not judge her too harshly , as she was very young at the time.","translation":"او را خیلی سخت قضاوت نکنید، زیرا او در آن زمان بسیار جوان بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001973827.mp3"}]'::jsonb,11),
('c5b2dea3-fe9c-5586-859d-fa655c6f711d','c3ae5491-923d-58ed-805e-93b4e76479d5',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'judging by/from something','داوری کردن، قضاوت کردن (پس از سنجش)؛ ارزیابی کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be difficult/hard to judge The economic results of the reforms are difficult to judge.','be impossible to judge How much this affected their children was impossible to judge.','judge something objectively (= by looking at the facts ) His behaviour, judged objectively by what he has done, is dishonest.','judge somebody harshly (= in a severe or unkind way ) Do not judge her too harshly; she was very young at the time.','judge something correctly It takes a lot of experience to judge correctly what is needed.','judge something a success/failure (= consider it to be a success/failure ) The concert was judged a success.','judge something on its merits (= according to what you see when you look at it, rather than what people tell you ) The arguments should be judged on their merits.','judge something on the basis of something (= by considering something ) It is difficult to judge progress on the basis of a single day.','judge it best/better to do something (= think that something is the best thing to do ) Robert wanted to go and help him, but judged it best to stay where he was.','judge it safe to do something (= consider that it is safe to do something ) He listened for some time before judging it safe to go downstairs.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
