('7b3ae82e-42db-5f90-8f2c-8de7cce0d231','a1ba6fce-cd1b-5ef4-b96e-eaa3c35b74b5',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make sounds with your voice , usually while you are smiling , because you think something is funny','[ intransitive ]',null,'خندیدن؛ خنده (فرد)؛ خشم‌مند (از)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['burst out laughing (= suddenly start laughing ) She looked at him and burst out laughing.','make somebody laugh I like Ron, he makes me laugh.','begin/start to laugh He suddenly began to laugh.','want to laugh (= to feel like laughing, even though it might be more polite not to ) He was so earnest that I wanted to laugh.','try not to laugh (= to not laugh, even though something is funny, because it would not be polite ) ‘Are you all right?’ Amy said, trying not to laugh.','fall about laughing British English (= laugh a lot ) He saw the look on my face and he just fell about laughing.','laugh hysterically (= laugh so much that you cannot stop, because you find something extremely funny ) The people at the next table were laughing hysterically at us.','laugh heartily especially written (= laugh a lot ) Misha laughed heartily throughout the play.','laugh out loud/aloud (= laugh so that other people can hear you ) Some parts of the book were so funny that they made me laugh out loud.','laugh your head off (= laugh a lot ) The audience laughed its head off all the way through.','laugh till you cry/laugh till the tears run down your face He leaned back in his chair and laughed till the tears ran down his face.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Maria looked at him and laughed.","translation":"ماریا به او نگاه کرد و خندید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001744162.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘I didn’t know what I was doing, ’ she said, laughing at the memory.","translation":"او با خنده به خاطره گفت: \"من نمی دانستم دارم چه کار می کنم.\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001481165.mp3"},{"sentence":"Tony was laughing so hard he had to steady himself on the table.","translation":"تونی آنقدر می خندید که مجبور شد خودش را روی میز ثابت کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001481162.mp3"},{"sentence":"Nora laughed so much that she nearly cried.","translation":"نورا آنقدر خندید که نزدیک بود گریه کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001828602.mp3"},{"sentence":"The kids tumbled around on the floor, laughing hysterically.","translation":"بچه ها روی زمین غلت خوردند و هیستریک می خندیدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001744170.mp3"},{"sentence":"He couldn’t help it; he burst out laughing (= suddenly started laughing ) .","translation":"او نمی توانست کمکی کند؛ از خنده منفجر شد (= ناگهان شروع به خندیدن کرد ) .","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001481169.mp3"},{"sentence":"He’s one of the few writers who can make me laugh out loud .","translation":"او یکی از معدود نویسندگانی است که می تواند مرا با صدای بلند بخنداند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001744180.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('16daf42e-c73d-5821-981b-ace993f5d3fa','a1ba6fce-cd1b-5ef4-b96e-eaa3c35b74b5',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to say something in a voice that shows you are amused','[ transitive ]',null,'برای گفتن چیزی با صدایی که نشان می دهد شما سرگرم هستید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['burst out laughing (= suddenly start laughing ) She looked at him and burst out laughing.','make somebody laugh I like Ron, he makes me laugh.','begin/start to laugh He suddenly began to laugh.','want to laugh (= to feel like laughing, even though it might be more polite not to ) He was so earnest that I wanted to laugh.','try not to laugh (= to not laugh, even though something is funny, because it would not be polite ) ‘Are you all right?’ Amy said, trying not to laugh.','fall about laughing British English (= laugh a lot ) He saw the look on my face and he just fell about laughing.','laugh hysterically (= laugh so much that you cannot stop, because you find something extremely funny ) The people at the next table were laughing hysterically at us.','laugh heartily especially written (= laugh a lot ) Misha laughed heartily throughout the play.','laugh out loud/aloud (= laugh so that other people can hear you ) Some parts of the book were so funny that they made me laugh out loud.','laugh your head off (= laugh a lot ) The audience laughed its head off all the way through.','laugh till you cry/laugh till the tears run down your face He leaned back in his chair and laughed till the tears ran down his face.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘You look ridiculous!’ Nick laughed.","translation":"نیک خندید: «مسخره به نظر می‌رسی!»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001481181.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
