('2647ea1b-dc85-5b67-952b-a37da819321c','7e651251-99ea-53a0-aa4f-4fe2ba71e6c4',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the act of laughing or the sound you make when you laugh','[ countable ]',null,'خنده، قهقهه؛ نشانه شادی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give/let out a laugh She gave a loud laugh.','get a laugh ( also draw a laugh British English written ) (= be laughed at ) Most of his jokes didn’t even get a laugh.','get a laugh out of somebody (= make someone laugh ) I always managed to get a laugh out of my audience.','have a laugh about/at/over something (= laugh about something ) The farmer had a good laugh at our attempts to catch the horse.','I could use a laugh (= I want to hear something funny to cheer me up ) Tell me what she said - I could use a laugh.','a good laugh We all got a good laugh out of it later.','a big laugh There was a big laugh from the crowd.','a short/little/small laugh He let out a nervous little laugh.','a loud/soft laugh He let out a loud laugh when he heard what had happened.','a belly laugh (= a deep loud laugh ) It’s the kind of comedy that raises a smile rather than a belly laugh.','a hearty laugh (= a loud laugh that shows you really enjoyed something ) With a hearty laugh, he began to tell the story.','a nervous laugh ‘Don’t be silly, ’ she said with a nervous laugh.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He gave a short laugh.","translation":"خنده کوتاهی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000923.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘What a mess!’ she said, with a laugh.","translation":"با خنده گفت: \"چه بهم ریخته!\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001744192.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('889b62c5-e697-55f5-827d-e6610f43b669','7e651251-99ea-53a0-aa4f-4fe2ba71e6c4',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if something is a laugh, you have fun and enjoy yourself when you are doing it','[ countable ]',null,'اگر چیزی خنده است، از انجام آن لذت می برید و لذت می برید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give/let out a laugh She gave a loud laugh.','get a laugh ( also draw a laugh British English written ) (= be laughed at ) Most of his jokes didn’t even get a laugh.','get a laugh out of somebody (= make someone laugh ) I always managed to get a laugh out of my audience.','have a laugh about/at/over something (= laugh about something ) The farmer had a good laugh at our attempts to catch the horse.','I could use a laugh (= I want to hear something funny to cheer me up ) Tell me what she said - I could use a laugh.','a good laugh We all got a good laugh out of it later.','a big laugh There was a big laugh from the crowd.','a short/little/small laugh He let out a nervous little laugh.','a loud/soft laugh He let out a loud laugh when he heard what had happened.','a belly laugh (= a deep loud laugh ) It’s the kind of comedy that raises a smile rather than a belly laugh.','a hearty laugh (= a loud laugh that shows you really enjoyed something ) With a hearty laugh, he began to tell the story.','a nervous laugh ‘Don’t be silly, ’ she said with a nervous laugh.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We all went to the beach last night – it was a really good laugh .","translation":"همه ما دیشب به ساحل رفتیم - خنده واقعاً خوبی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001744219.mp3"},{"sentence":"The other campers were nice, and we had a great laugh together.","translation":"بقیه کمپینگ ها خوب بودند و با هم کلی خندیدیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001979732.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was a great holiday with lots of laughs .","translation":"تعطیلات عالی بود با خنده های فراوان.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001979736.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('cae00be6-b4f6-52ad-b70b-cd7369298743','7e651251-99ea-53a0-aa4f-4fe2ba71e6c4',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'somebody is a (good) laugh','خنده، قهقهه؛ نشانه شادی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give/let out a laugh She gave a loud laugh.','get a laugh ( also draw a laugh British English written ) (= be laughed at ) Most of his jokes didn’t even get a laugh.','get a laugh out of somebody (= make someone laugh ) I always managed to get a laugh out of my audience.','have a laugh about/at/over something (= laugh about something ) The farmer had a good laugh at our attempts to catch the horse.','I could use a laugh (= I want to hear something funny to cheer me up ) Tell me what she said - I could use a laugh.','a good laugh We all got a good laugh out of it later.','a big laugh There was a big laugh from the crowd.','a short/little/small laugh He let out a nervous little laugh.','a loud/soft laugh He let out a loud laugh when he heard what had happened.','a belly laugh (= a deep loud laugh ) It’s the kind of comedy that raises a smile rather than a belly laugh.','a hearty laugh (= a loud laugh that shows you really enjoyed something ) With a hearty laugh, he began to tell the story.','a nervous laugh ‘Don’t be silly, ’ she said with a nervous laugh.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
