('4b54d74a-0f8c-5996-89fe-c8ad41d20bce','3cee29a2-fd4f-59dd-8ae3-d28d1719ea41',1,'when it is dark','وقتی هوا تاریک است','spoken & written','the dark part of each 24-hour period when the sun cannot be seen and when most people sleep',null,null,'شب، شبانه؛ شب (سرنشین)؛ شب (عروسی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['last night It rained last night.','tomorrow night I should be back by tomorrow night.','Friday/Saturday etc night I haven’t seen him since Thursday night.','an early night (= when you go to bed early ) I’m really tired - I need an early night.','a late night (= when you go to bed late ) We had a late night last night.','a long night (= a night when you do not sleep or you work hard ) Everyone was tired and grumpy. It had been a long night.','a sleepless night She had spent a sleepless night wondering what to do.','spend a night somewhere (= sleep somewhere ) We spent two nights at the Grand Hotel.','stay the night (= sleep at someone’s house ) You’re welcome to stay the night if you like.','have a bad night (= not sleep well, especially when you are ill ) I had a bad night last night.','night falls written (= it starts to become dark ) It grew colder as night fell.','the night wears on (= continues ) The pain gradually got better as the night wore on.','the night sky We looked up at the stars in the night sky.','the night air The night air was scented with jasmine.','a night train/bus/flight I took the night train to Fort William.','all night He looked as if he’d been up all night.','all night long (= used to emphasize that something continues for the whole night ) The noise continued all night long!','late at night We often get to bed very late at night.','at this time of night (= used when something happens very late at night, and you are surprised ) Why are you calling me at this time of night?','late/far into the night (= until very late at night ) Staff worked late into the night to make necessary repairs.','in the middle of the night She woke up suddenly in the middle of the night.','in/at the dead of night literary (= in the middle of the night when it is quiet ) He drove through the countryside in the dead of night.','day and night/night and day (= all the time ) The phones rang day and night.','morning, noon, and night (= all the time ) She nagged at him morning, noon, and night.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"It was a cold moonlit night.","translation":"یک شب سرد مهتابی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001701968.mp3"},{"sentence":"I didn’t sleep too well last night.","translation":"دیشب خیلی خوب نخوابیدم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000242200.mp3"},{"sentence":"At night the temperature drops below zero.","translation":"در شب درجه حرارت به زیر صفر می رسد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001760930.mp3"},{"sentence":"He woke up twice during the night.","translation":"او در طول شب دو بار از خواب بیدار شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-002007695.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many animals hunt by night.","translation":"بسیاری از حیوانات در شب شکار می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001760933.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was a storm on Friday night.","translation":"جمعه شب طوفان بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001100.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('ebeb21da-c172-52cb-b631-9d4196f8c03d','3cee29a2-fd4f-59dd-8ae3-d28d1719ea41',2,'evening','عصر','spoken & written','the time during the evening until you go to bed',null,null,'زمان در طول شب تا زمانی که به رختخواب بروید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['last night It rained last night.','tomorrow night I should be back by tomorrow night.','Friday/Saturday etc night I haven’t seen him since Thursday night.','an early night (= when you go to bed early ) I’m really tired - I need an early night.','a late night (= when you go to bed late ) We had a late night last night.','a long night (= a night when you do not sleep or you work hard ) Everyone was tired and grumpy. It had been a long night.','a sleepless night She had spent a sleepless night wondering what to do.','spend a night somewhere (= sleep somewhere ) We spent two nights at the Grand Hotel.','stay the night (= sleep at someone’s house ) You’re welcome to stay the night if you like.','have a bad night (= not sleep well, especially when you are ill ) I had a bad night last night.','night falls written (= it starts to become dark ) It grew colder as night fell.','the night wears on (= continues ) The pain gradually got better as the night wore on.','the night sky We looked up at the stars in the night sky.','the night air The night air was scented with jasmine.','a night train/bus/flight I took the night train to Fort William.','all night He looked as if he’d been up all night.','all night long (= used to emphasize that something continues for the whole night ) The noise continued all night long!','late at night We often get to bed very late at night.','at this time of night (= used when something happens very late at night, and you are surprised ) Why are you calling me at this time of night?','late/far into the night (= until very late at night ) Staff worked late into the night to make necessary repairs.','in the middle of the night She woke up suddenly in the middle of the night.','in/at the dead of night literary (= in the middle of the night when it is quiet ) He drove through the countryside in the dead of night.','day and night/night and day (= all the time ) The phones rang day and night.','morning, noon, and night (= all the time ) She nagged at him morning, noon, and night.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We had a really good meal last night .","translation":"دیشب واقعا یک غذای خوب خوردیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702008.mp3"},{"sentence":"They stay in and watch television every night .","translation":"آنها هر شب در آنجا می مانند و تلویزیون تماشا می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702011.mp3"},{"sentence":"She recognised him from the night before (= the previous evening ) .","translation":"او را از شب قبل (= عصر قبل) شناخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702014.mp3"},{"sentence":"My parents are coming for dinner tomorrow night .","translation":"پدر و مادرم فردا شب برای شام می آیند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000242243.mp3"},{"sentence":"There’s a party at Ben’s place on Saturday night.","translation":"شنبه شب یک مهمانی در محل بن برگزار می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000242251.mp3"},{"sentence":"We were on our way back from a night out (= an evening when you go to a party, restaurant, theatre etc ) at the theatre.","translation":"ما در راه بازگشت از یک شب بیرون رفتن (= عصری که به مهمانی، رستوران، تئاتر و غیره می روید) در تئاتر بودیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001702020.mp3"},{"sentence":"Anna doesn’t like him walking home late at night .","translation":"آنا دوست ندارد تا دیروقت به خانه راه برود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000242258.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
